# Garmin MCP server configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Real process environment variables
# always win over this file. Any variable set to an EMPTY string counts as
# unset, so a bare `FOO=` placeholder falls through to the `_FILE` or
# interactive fallback instead of submitting an empty value.

# --- Credentials (layer 3: SSO login) ----------------------------------------
# Either the value directly...
GARMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
GARMIN_PASSWORD=your-password

# ...or a path to a file containing it, which keeps the secret out of the
# process environment. Takes effect only when the direct variable is unset.
#GARMIN_EMAIL_FILE=/run/secrets/garmin_email
#GARMIN_PASSWORD_FILE=/run/secrets/garmin_password

# --- MFA ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# If the account has MFA enabled the server prompts on stdin by default. For a
# non-interactive run (a backgrounded process, an agent-driven test) supply the
# code up front, or point at a file that is polled for five minutes so the
# time-sensitive code can be injected after the run starts. The file is deleted
# only once Garmin has accepted the code.
#GARMIN_MFA_CODE=123456
#GARMIN_MFA_CODE_FILE=.mfa_code.txt

# --- Session cache -----------------------------------------------------------
# A successful login is cached (0600) so MFA is not needed on every start. The
# default path is `.di_session.json` relative to the working directory, which a
# desktop MCP client may set to anywhere — pin it with an absolute path.
#GARMIN_SESSION_FILE=/home/you/.config/garmin-mcp/di_session.json

# --- Optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Skip the SSO login entirely by supplying a service ticket (layer 2).
#GARMIN_SERVICE_TICKET=ST-...

# Override the auto-detected Garmin handle if the profile probe cannot find it.
#GARMIN_DISPLAY_NAME=your-garmin-handle
